// c-callsite-01: CallSite::raise_throws returns early when the callee's
// `throws` is an open cell, so a call through a `fn(..) throws 'e`
// parameter raises nothing to the enclosing catch or to the definition's
// inferred throws.
//
// command: graphix --no-cache design/review-2026-10-05/repro/c-callsite-01.gx
//
// expected: refused by the check (`--check` included). f(x) raises 'e, so
// h throws 'e and h(g, 0) throws Error<ErrChain<`Boom>>; the handler must be
// refused as it is when h declares `-> i64 throws 'e`:
//   c is i64 and cannot hold Error<ErrChain<`Boom>>
//
// observed: `--check` exits 0, and h's inferred signature is
// fn(f: fn(x: i64) -> i64 throws 'e, x: i64) -> i64, with no throws. At run
// time the error reaches the catch anyway and `c: i64` holds it:
//   default (JIT): thread 'tokio-rt-worker' panicked at
//     graphix-compiler/src/fusion/kernel.rs:243:13: kernel param `c`:
//     runtime Error(..) does not match the compiled Scalar(I64) slot
//     Error: runtime did not respond  (exit 1)
//   --no-fusion: arith error .. at line: 37, column: 25 "can't add error types"
//   graphix-fuzz check: the same panic, aborts (core dumped, exit 134)
// The same skip types a catch INSIDE such a function as bottom: with
// `let caught: bool = never(); catch(e) caught <- e; f(x); caught` as h's
// body, `--check` passes and the run prints error:[.. "Boom" ..] as the
// value of `caught`.
let h = |f: fn(x: i64) -> i64 throws 'e, x: i64| f(x);

let g = |x: i64| -> i64 select x {
    0 => error(`Boom)?,
    x => x
};

let c: i64 = never();
catch(e) c <- e;
h(g, 0);

let k = |n: i64| -> i64 n * 2 + 1;
k(c)
